# No check-ID rules. A line beginning with `!` suppresses a check or a check
# family repo-wide, permanently and invisibly, and pre-waives checks that do not
# exist yet. It is also the mechanism #455 describes as attacker-controllable on
# download paths. Disposition of a specific finding belongs in the issue tracker,
# not here. Path rules below are a scope statement and are disclosed on the
# `Scope` line of every scan. `__tests__/hmaignore-scope-only.test.ts` enforces this.
#
# No shipped path is excluded. The only whole-path rules are the three test
# trees; everything under `src/`, `scripts/` and the root documents is scanned
# by our own build. A finding on shipped source that is the file's own
# construction is declared below as `<file>:<CHECK-ID> # <reason>`, one file and
# one check per line, so every other check still runs on that file and the
# `--json` report still counts what each line matched.

# Intentionally vulnerable test fixtures — git-only, excluded from scans and npm publish
test-fixtures/
test/

# Test files contain intentional attack patterns and vulnerable code samples
__tests__/

# By-construction findings on shipped files, each narrowed to one file and one check.
src/hardening/scanner.ts:UNICODE-STEGO-002 # the display sanitiser skips the variation-selector and tag-character ranges (0xFE00..0xFE0F, 0xE0000..0xE01EF) by codepoint, and that range literal next to a .codePointAt read is the decoder shape the check looks for; a detector firing on its own countermeasure, same class as #468
src/nanomind-core/analyzers/stego-analyzer.ts:UNICODE-STEGO-002 # the steganography range table lists the variation-selector and tag-character ranges (0xFE00..0xFE0F, 0xE0000..0xE01EF) it detects, so the table reads as a decoder; a detector firing on its own countermeasure, same class as #468
src/nanomind-core/analyzers/stego-analyzer.ts:UNICODE-STEGO-005 # the homoglyph table names each Cyrillic codepoint with its glyph in a trailing comment, and those glyphs are the confusables the check detects; #468
src/nanomind-core/inference/tme-classifier.ts:AST-CRED-003 # the three 64-hex values are the SHA-256 pins each downloaded model file is checked against before it is loaded; an integrity digest, not a credential
CHANGELOG.md:UNICODE-STEGO-002 # release notes describing the decoder detector spell decoder ranges in hex and decimal next to the words .codePointAt and eval; a release note decodes nothing, see #467
